.h-full.flex.flex-col
  h1.pb-4.text-gray-500.text-base.sm:text-lg.md:text-xl.lg:text-2xl.flex-shrink-0.hidden.sm:block
    = t('layout.notifications')

  / A phone has the rows in a white card on the gray page, like a grouped
    list. The desktop has them on its white box, where a negative margin lets
    the hover reach past the content edge, so the text still aligns with the
    heading above.
  ul.max-lg:overflow-clip.max-lg:rounded-xl.max-lg:bg-surface.lg:-mx-3.lg:overflow-y-auto.lg:flex-1
    - notifications.each do |notification|
      = render Notification::Item::Component.new(notification:)
